          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: लिपिक",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "लिपिक — lipik — \"a clerk\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "लिपिकाने माझा अर्ज वाचला. lipikāne mājhā arja vāclā. The clerk read my application."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "लिपिक (lipik) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit lipika, \"a scribe, a clerk\" (Monier-Williams), built on lipi, \"writing\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
